<p><b>Achzizra's Bio:</b>
<table border=1 width=400>
  <tr><td>
  The Iksar turns to face you. <br> "<I>Kahss, s'ske Navi mass a'ak ji...</I>" <br>The Iksar frowns, studying you from underneath the skull she wears for a helmet. "I see you do not understand the language of the Ancients. I did not really expect one like you would, but for some things, no other language will suffice."<br> She makes as if leaving, but stops, tail twitching impatiently. <br>"The skull. Before my Rebirth I ripped my father's head off his shoulders and made his skull into this helm of dishonor. He ran off to be with the outcasts. My mother offered herself up on the altar of Terror that I might live in this shame. What became of my fellow broodlings I do not know, for it happened not long before my Rebirth, and the start of my service as a Shaman of Fear." She pauses. "I was weak then, but I have grown stronger."<br> The Iksar looks up at the setting sun, and the blood red gibbous moon with all its ill omens. With a few mouthed words and a quick movement of the hand she forces a spirit inside your body, you feel it enter you without meeting resistance. The Iksar grins, revealing rows of sharp teeth. You can still not read anything from her dead black eyes. "It is time for you to leave, stranger. <I>A'ak Nazar</I>, the night welcomes you.. But is it a friendly welcome, or the welcome of a hungry nibbler to a broodling fresh from Rebirth? I shall hold it off long enough for you to escape. Perhaps."<br> As you run for safety with the aid of the spirit, you can hear the laughter of the Iksar, a soft sound like spring rain. 
